-- BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000266 BREACH-DOCTOR-1, ANTIFRAGILE-1: a single executor on a critical path ships with its second path). Companion of
-- qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0 (jobBreachDoctorWatch, qnfo-cloud-ops/breach-doctor-watch.test.mjs).
-- The breach doctor (migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql, qnfo-fleet-control breachDoctorTick) is worker code on the */10 slot and writes its own metrics, so a stalled fleet-control tick or a stalled
-- doctor block would stop the doctor and the numbers that report it together. State read 2026-10-26T10:52Z (SELECT only): the doctor migration is applied (migration_runs id 606, ok, 10:22:09Z) and ops_config
-- breach_doctor = on; breach_diagnosis_events exists with 3 tick events, the newest at 10:50:49Z; metric_registry doctor_tick_age_min is MEASURED (last_value 10, last_refreshed 10:50:49Z, the second of the newest tick,
-- so written by the doctor itself: this watch is not deployed yet); spof_registry holds the doctor row with a 'planned:' alternate_path, alternate_tested_at NULL and issue_id 1000397; control_registry
-- breach-doctor-switch exists with alternate_tested_at NULL and issue_id 1000397; agent_issues 1000397 (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1) is open, high, and its active contract issue-1000397 reads cloud_ops_events kind 'job-run'
-- for job 'breach-doctor-watch'; no cloud_ops_events row of kind breach-doctor-watch exists. The second path is qnfo-cloud-ops: on every 10-minute tick of a different worker and a different cron it
-- reads the newest 'tick' event of the doctor, writes doctor_tick_age_min from it, and when the age passes 30 minutes files one deduped issue "BREACH-DOCTOR-1: doctor stalled (watch)" (at most one per 120
-- minutes) whose d1-query contract closes it when the tick is 15 minutes old or less. A missing ledger table or ops_config breach_doctor = off makes it skip without writing (the tolerance stays for a failed or
-- rolled-back doctor migration). Order of events: CI applies this file when the PR merges, before the canonical deploy of qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0 has run and its canary passed, and nothing writes a breach-doctor-watch
-- event until the first watch tick after that deploy.
-- What this file does (INSERT OR IGNORE and guarded UPDATE only, nothing deleted, alternate_tested_at never written):
--   * spof_registry: the doctor tick row (the same component text the doctor migration uses) gets the watch as its alternate_path. The row is inserted when absent, and a 'planned:' alternate_path written by
--     the doctor migration is replaced by what was built (the watch notices and reports a stall; it runs no playbook). Both migration orders end in the same row. alternate_tested_at stays NULL until a drill passes.
--   * spof_alternate_probes: one read-only expected/observed probe the chaos drill (every 360 minutes) judges and, on a pass, stamps spof_registry.alternate_tested_at (qnfo-fleet-control chaosDrill, unchanged). It passes
--     only when the doctor ledger exists, a breach-doctor-watch event answered inside 30 minutes and doctor_tick_age_min reads 30 or less (the closing probe of the package), and it fails with the reason on each
--     missing piece, including the gap between this file (applied at merge) and the first watch tick after the worker deploys: no pass by absence. A drill that runs in that gap files one CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 issue that its next pass closes.
--   * failure mode breach-doctor-watch-silent with its fm- detector contract: the doctor ledger exists, breach_doctor is not off, the failure mode row and the switch row are both older than 30 minutes (the grace for the deploy that follows this file) and no breach-doctor-watch event is 30 minutes old.
--   * agent_issues 1000397 (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1) is narrowed to the half that is not built and stays OPEN: guarded UPDATEs of its description (the Definition of done line), of its active contract issue-1000397 (the probe) and of
--     control_registry breach-doctor-switch (alternate_path says the watch is built, not a separate package). Status is not touched, nothing is closed and nothing is superseded.
--   * a capability_ledger row and two decision_log rows.
-- Not in this file (the doctor migration owns them): the doctor tables, metrics, triggers and the issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 itself. That issue asks for more than this package builds: besides a heartbeat it has the watch
-- run the validated per-issue playbooks when the tick is stale and it stamps alternate_tested_at on spof_registry and on control_registry breach-doctor-switch. Its contract probe reads cloud_ops_events kind 'job-run' for
-- job 'breach-doctor-watch', and this job writes kind 'breach-doctor-watch' (a fixed-id heartbeat, or a file-* row) and never a job-run row on a tick (only runScheduledJob and POST /run write those). The probe could therefore
-- not pass on the delivered half, and a manual POST /run would close the issue on a heartbeat while the playbook half is unbuilt. So the issue is not closed on a heartbeat and not left with an unpassable probe: it is narrowed
-- to the acting half and probes that half (control_registry breach-doctor-switch alternate_tested_at set, and a capability_ledger row breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks, which the change that builds the acting half writes).
-- spof-review: no new cron, worker or binding; the watch rides qnfo-cloud-ops's existing */10 tick (CRON-SINGLE-TRIGGER-1) and reads qnfo-audit through the AUDIT binding it already has.
-- charter-pillar: autonomy. No new table family.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: DELETE FROM spof_alternate_probes WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND window_note LIKE '30 minutes for the watch heartbeat%'; UPDATE spof_registry SET alternate_path = 'planned: qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1) reads doctor_tick_age_min; rolled back', alternate_tested_at = NULL WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND alternate_path LIKE 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch%'; DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-breach-doctor-watch-silent'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'breach-doctor-watch-silent'; DELETE FROM capability_ledger WHERE capability = 'breach-doctor:second-path-watch'; UPDATE agent_issues SET description = substr(description, 1, instr(description, 'Scope narrowed 2026-10-26 by the BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 package') - 1) || 'Definition of done: a cloud_ops_events job-run row for job breach-doctor-watch is under 120 minutes old (the closing probe of this issue) and the spof_registry row names the tested alternate.' WHERE id = (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) AND instr(description, 'Scope narrowed 2026-10-26 by the BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 package') > 0; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET precondition = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: the doctor tick is the only runner of the diagnosis path', action = replace('a session adds jobBreachDoctorWatch to qnfo-cloud-ops@@ the stale-PR lane merges it and the canonical deploy ships it', '@@', char(59)), verify_probe = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''job-run'' AND job = ''breach-doctor-watch'' AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'')) THEN ''no breach-doctor-watch job-run event in the last 120 minutes'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed' WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) AND instr(verify_probe, 'breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks') > 0; UPDATE control_registry SET alternate_path = replace(alternate_path, 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1, 1.39.0, built) reads the same switch and writes nothing while it is off, but runs no playbook yet, so this alternate stays untested until the acting half of issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 lands', 'the qnfo-cloud-ops watch (separate package) reads the same switch'), evidence = replace(evidence, ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 2026-10-26: alternate_path now names the built job (qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0 jobBreachDoctorWatch) and leaves the alternate untested until the acting half of issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 lands', '') WHERE control = 'breach-doctor-switch'
-- Rollback note: the decision_log rows stay (append-only); an alternate_tested_at a passing drill stamped stays (it was earned); the worker change reverts with the canonical deploy canary.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO spof_registry (component, critical_path, alternate_path, alternate_tested_at, evidence) VALUES
 ('breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)', 'unowned breach -> diagnosis -> allowlisted action -> verified close',
  'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1, qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0): on every 10-minute tick of a different worker and a different cron it reads the newest breach_diagnosis_events tick, writes metric doctor_tick_age_min from it (a stalled doctor cannot hide behind its own metric) and, when the age passes 30 minutes, files one deduped issue "BREACH-DOCTOR-1: doctor stalled (watch)" (at most one per 120 minutes) whose d1-query contract closes it once the tick is 15 minutes old or less; every run writes a cloud_ops_events row of kind breach-doctor-watch. It makes no model call and runs no playbook: it notices and reports the stall, the diagnosis path itself keeps one runner, and the acting half (running the validated per-issue playbooks when the tick is stale) stays open as issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1.',
  NULL,
  'new 2026-10-26 (BREACH-DOCTOR-1, agent_issues 1000266): the doctor is worker code on the existing */10 slot of qnfo-fleet-control, no new cron, worker or binding; this row is written by the watch migration so the second path is on record whichever of the two migrations applies first');

UPDATE spof_registry SET alternate_path = 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1, qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0): on every 10-minute tick of a different worker and a different cron it reads the newest breach_diagnosis_events tick, writes metric doctor_tick_age_min from it (a stalled doctor cannot hide behind its own metric) and, when the age passes 30 minutes, files one deduped issue "BREACH-DOCTOR-1: doctor stalled (watch)" (at most one per 120 minutes) whose d1-query contract closes it once the tick is 15 minutes old or less; every run writes a cloud_ops_events row of kind breach-doctor-watch. It makes no model call and runs no playbook: it notices and reports the stall, the diagnosis path itself keeps one runner, and the acting half (running the validated per-issue playbooks when the tick is stale) stays open as issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1.',
  evidence = evidence || ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 2026-10-26 (agent_issues 1000266): alternate_path recorded with the job that implements it, replacing the planned text (the built job notices and reports a stall and runs no playbook); alternate_tested_at is stamped only by a passing chaos drill on the spof_alternate_probes row of this component, which reads a breach-doctor-watch event inside 30 minutes and doctor_tick_age_min at 30 or below'
WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND alternate_path LIKE 'planned:%';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO spof_alternate_probes (component, probe_sql, exercise, window_note, enabled) VALUES
 ('breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''table'' AND name = ''breach_diagnosis_events'') THEN ''the doctor ledger breach_diagnosis_events does not exist, so there is no doctor tick to watch yet'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''breach-doctor-watch'' AND status = ''ok'' AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-30 minutes'')) THEN ''no breach-doctor-watch event answered in 30 minutes, so the second path of the breach doctor has not run'' WHEN (SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'') IS NULL THEN ''doctor_tick_age_min has no value'' WHEN CAST((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'') AS REAL) > 30 THEN ''doctor_tick_age_min reads '' || (SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'') || '' minutes, above the limit of 30'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  NULL,
  '30 minutes for the watch heartbeat (qnfo-cloud-ops writes one breach-doctor-watch event on every 10-minute tick, three ticks of margin) and 30 minutes for the doctor tick age (doctor_tick_age_min, written by the watch from the doctor''s own tick events); the watch is the exercise: it runs on every tick, so the alternate is run, not declared',
  1);

